      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAn aborted setwise score request crashes the scheduler, taking down every in-flight request.\n\nSetwise scoring (#38965, CausalLM support in #41188) reads label scores at every `score_extraction_token_id` marker in a prompt, via the request's `token_indices_to_pool`. Only those requests carry pooling positions; for all others the field is `None`.\n\n`Req.set_finish_with_abort` shrinks the prompt to one token so the long prefill is skipped, but keeps `token_indices_to_pool`. The logits processor then reads positions past that one token and hits `vectorized gather kernel index out of bounds` (`CUDA error: device-side assert triggered`). Any abort path triggers it, the easiest being a prompt longer than the context.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Clear `token_indices_to_pool` in `set_finish_with_abort`, next to the existing one-token prompt reset. Requests without pooling positions are unaffected.\n- Unit test in `test_setwise_score_mixin.py` that fails on main and passes with the fix.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nStock `Qwen3.5-2B` with setwise scoring (`--disable-radix-cache --chunked-prefill-size -1 --max-total-tokens 4096`), on 1xH100. A 200-token request, then a 6,010-token one, then the 200-token one again:\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| over-length request | scheduler crashes, engine killed | `ValueError: Input length (6010 tokens) exceeds the maximum allowed length (4090 tokens)` |\n| next request | no server | same scores as the first request |\n\nTested on a v0.5.22 build with main's sources.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance impact: one attribute assignment on the abort path.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). No documentation change needed.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41757397988](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757397988)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41757397803](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757397803)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41757397844](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41757397844)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, o